# Normalize on commit, check out LF everywhere.
#
# This is a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise
# write CRLF into the working tree. Two things break when it does: shell
# scripts refuse to run under Linux bash, and any byte-exact comparison
# between a file here and the same file elsewhere fails on invisible
# differences. The sibling `branch` repo learned this the expensive way --
# its migration checksums are sha256 over raw bytes with no newline
# normalization, so the same file hashed differently on Windows and Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
